{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new recipes and functions to extend the capabilities of more-itertools, including polynomial evaluation and derivative tools, relative seeking for seekable objects, and indexing for combinations. It also corrects behaviors in existing functions like `unique_in_window` and `partial_product`, and adds new iteration utilities such as `nth_combination_with_replacement`. Please ensure all public APIs behave according to the specifications below.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m04",
      "text": "The `seekable` object must support a `relative_seek` method that advances the current position by a specified number of items relative to the current location. This operation should raise an error if the resulting position would be invalid or out of bounds."
    },
    {
      "id": "m06",
      "text": "New functions `combination_index`, `combination_with_replacement_index`, `permutation_index`, and `product_index` must return the zero-based index of a given combination, permutation, or product within its lexicographically sorted sequence. These functions should accept iterable inputs and return integer indices corresponding to their positions."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "The `polynomial_eval` function must evaluate a polynomial defined by a list of coefficients at a given value. It should return the computed numerical result based on standard polynomial evaluation rules."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10",
      "text": "The `nth_combination_with_replacement` function must return the nth combination with replacement from an input iterable, using zero-based indexing. It should raise an error if n is negative or exceeds the total number of possible combinations."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "The `sum_of_squares` function must compute the sum of the squares of elements in an iterable. It should handle numeric inputs correctly and return a single numerical result."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "The `iterate` function must yield successive results of applying a function to an accumulator and the next item from an iterable. The first yielded value should be the initial accumulator value provided by the user."
    },
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The `partial_product` function must generate Cartesian products of input iterables up to a specified length, behaving consistently with `itertools.product` but allowing for partial lengths. It should correctly handle cases where the requested length exceeds the available combinations without raising errors unexpectedly."
    },
    {
      "id": "m19",
      "text": "The `unique_in_window` function must yield unique items from an iterable, ensuring that each item appears only once within the current sliding window of size n. It should maintain the order of first appearance within the window and update the window state correctly as it iterates."
    },
    {
      "id": "m20",
      "text": "The `polynomial_derivative` function must compute the derivative of a polynomial defined by a list of coefficients. It should return a new list of coefficients representing the derivative polynomial."
    },
    {
      "id": "m22",
      "text": "Ensure compatibility with Python version 10.0.0 requirements for functions such as `batched`, `convolve`, `factor`, `matmul`, `numeric_range`, `sieve`, and `transpose`. These functions must operate correctly under the updated environment constraints without deprecation warnings or runtime errors."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that these changes integrate smoothly with existing functionality and do not introduce regressions. Documentation updates should reflect any new parameters or return types described above."
}
